  "family": "SnakeYAML via circe-yaml (Scala wrapper: SnakeYAML 2.2 compose plus circe-yaml node-to-Json conversion)",
  "family_note": "Not an independent YAML parser. circe-yaml's Parser calls new Yaml(new SafeConstructor(loaderOptions)).compose(reader) and converts the composed SnakeYAML node graph to circe Json in its own Scala code (resolved tags to numbers, booleans and null, merge-key flattening, string keys). It shares the SnakeYAML family with the selected snakeyaml path (pinned here to SnakeYAML 2.2, the version circe-yaml 0.16.1 declares) and with the jackson-dataformat-yaml lead. The Scala 2.12 (170) and Scala 3 (94) cross-builds of the same source are separate Maven artifacts with their own deps.dev counts; they are not summed or counted again. circe-yaml-v12 (SnakeYAML Engine backend) is a separate artifact, not run.",
  "configuration_note": "Default parser (Parser.default: maxAliasesForCollections 50, nestingDepthLimit 50, default codePointLimit). circe Json numbers do not keep the YAML int/float tag: the adapter types a number with an exact Long value as int and any other as float; the controls contain no integral-valued floats, so this cannot change the result.",
